# tools/al/ales_stereo_compress_env_hold_witness.rish — stereo_compress_env_hold: the attack/hold/release compressor carried into stereo, the linked held envelope driving one linked gain over time (ALES166).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES166.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-072211_fill-ales166-lotus-stereo-compress-env-hold.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_hold_env.rye (ALES165 — the linked held follower, its stereo_env_step_hold reused whole), lotus/stereo_compress_env.rye (ALES161 — the un-held linked compressor this reduces to at a hold of zero),
# lotus/compress_env_hold.rye (ALES58 — the mono attack/hold/release compressor, its CompressEnvHoldError reused whole and its output the left-always-peak comparison), lotus/compress.rye (ALES50 — the softened ceiling),
# lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 — the StereoClip), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_max, max_clip).
#
# lotus/stereo_compress_env_hold.rye compresses a span of sample-PAIRS in a master above a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one gain reduction following the shared LINKED HELD envelope over time. Each pair advances one
# shared envelope with one shared hold countdown toward the linked peak max(|left|, |right|) by ALES165's step (attack while rising and rearming the shared hold, the peak pinned while the countdown lasts, release once it
# expires): within the threshold both pass byte for byte, above it the softened target comp = threshold + excess·den/num (ALES50's ceiling on the linked held envelope) yields one gain comp/e applied to both raw samples —
# one detector, one hold, one gain, the image held. CompressEnvHoldError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadHold, BadRange) reused whole; the fusion adds no fault. Values only, never a length. The crux is the zero-hold
# law (a hold of zero reducing it to ALES161's stereo_compress_env byte for byte on both — the held rung's no-hold limit exactly the un-held one already proven), the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with
# left' equal to ALES58's mono compress_env_hold(left), the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel compress_env_hold differing), the image law (the shared gain preserving the L:R ratio, an out-of-phase
# pair returning still out of phase), the knob / no-pump laws (unit ratio the identity, a nonzero hold keeping the gain engaged across a duck rather than pumping), the carry law (a span in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal
# to the whole once on both, env and hold_left carrying), and the sub-threshold/silence/balance/atomicity/degenerate law.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_compress_env_hold_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-compress-env-hold: Language EN — stereo_compress_env_hold compresses a span of sample-pairs in a stereo master above a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one gain reduction following the shared linked held envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope with one shared hold countdown toward the linked peak (the max of the two channels' magnitudes, clamped to the rail): the attack fraction while it rises and rearms the shared hold, the peak pinned while the countdown lasts, the release only once it expires; where the held envelope sits within the threshold both channels pass byte for byte, and where it rises above, the envelope's excess is softened by the ratio and the single gain (the softened target over the envelope) is applied to both raw samples. It validates the threshold, ratio, attack, release, hold, and span once against the shared length before any write, so a refusal never compresses one channel and leaves the other torn. It writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced; the caller owns the envelope and the countdown across calls, so a span compressed in two pieces equals the whole once even when the split falls mid-hold."
say "ales-stereo-compress-env-hold: Style Radiant — ALES161 carried the breathing compressor into stereo: one shared envelope leaning in over the attack and easing back over the release, one softened gain applied to both channels so the image never pumps. Yet an un-held compressor still lets its gain jump back toward unity the moment a loud passage momentarily ducks below the threshold — it pumps, and the ear hears the gain breathe in and out on the whole field at once. A real compressor carries a hold knob for exactly this: on a fall away from a peak, it pins the peak for a little while before the release begins, so the gain reduction stays engaged through the duck. ALES165 built that hold stage inside the linked follower and proved it once. This rung spends that proof: it drives ALES50's softened ceiling from the linked held envelope rather than the plain linked one — the same stereo compressor, now with the patience that keeps it from pumping the image. It is the stereo mirror of ALES58's held mono compressor. Two proofs fused: the detector is the linked held follower (one shared envelope, one shared hold countdown pinning the linked peak across a fall so the two channels never release on different samples), and the gain is linked (one softened gain from the linked held envelope applied to both). The crux is six laws: the zero-hold law (a hold of zero making the linked held follower the plain linked follower, so this equals ALES161's stereo_compress_env byte for byte on both — the held rung's no-hold limit exactly the un-held rung already proven); the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with the left equal to ALES58's mono compress_env_hold of it byte for byte, the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel compress_env_hold genuinely differing); the image law (the shared gain preserving the left-to-right ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase, no magnitude expanding and no sign flipping); the knob and no-pump laws (unit ratio the identity everywhere, and a nonzero hold keeping the gain reduction engaged across a brief duck — the held magnitude no larger than the un-held one and strictly quieter at the duck, the pumping avoided); the carry law (a span compressed in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal to compressing the whole once, byte for byte on both); and the sub-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate law (a master whose linked held envelope never crosses the threshold passing byte for byte, silence staying silence, the lengths held, each of the five refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-compress-env-hold: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) carrying one shared i64 envelope and one shared u32 hold countdown, one linked-peak comparison and at most one multiply-then-divide for the held envelope step (ALES165's proven stereo_env_step_hold) plus one per channel for the gain, all in i64 (the product of a magnitude and the softened target at most 32768 times 32767 never overflowing), the gain comp over e in the half-open interval zero to one so every scaled magnitude is at most its input's and fits i16; the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (a compressor writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit, each written sign asserted held); the threshold, ratio, both coefficients, the hold, and the span are validated once before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never compresses one channel and leaves the other torn; the linked held envelope is asserted a legal magnitude in zero to sample_max each pair and the softened target within threshold to envelope, so the single gain is a genuine reduction; StereoCompressEnvHoldError is ALES58's CompressEnvHoldError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadHold, BadRange) reused whole, the fusion adding no fault. The zero-hold law is proven by running both stereo_compress_env_hold under a hold of zero and ALES161's un-held stereo_compress_env on the same master and demanding byte-for-byte equality on both channels; the linked-gain-over-time law against a master where the left always holds the peak — the left equal to ALES58's mono compress_env_hold of it byte for byte while the right is scaled by the same fraction, the independent mono compress_env_hold of the right alone shown to genuinely differ; the image law proves no magnitude expands and no sign flips over a mixed master and that an out-of-phase pair returns still exactly out of phase; the knob and no-pump laws prove unit ratio the identity everywhere and a nonzero hold keeping the gain engaged across a duck where an un-held compressor pumps; the carry law proves a span compressed in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal to the whole once on both channels; and the sub-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove a below-threshold master passing byte for byte, an all-silent master staying zero, the length held, each of the five refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the threshold a magnitude in sample units, the ratio a plain fraction, the attack, release, and hold per sample index, no real sample rate, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_compress_env_hold"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_compress_env_hold.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-compress-env-hold: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_compress_env_hold.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-compress-env-hold: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-compress-env-hold: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-compress-env-hold' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-compress-env-hold: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-compress-env-hold line"
